    "_comment": "Golden webhook-signature vectors shared by laravel-id (the sender) and every Cbox ID SDK that verifies (id-js, id-python, id-go, laravel-id-client). Each side used to re-implement the signing formula inside its own test, so flipping the signed string from \"{timestamp}.{body}\" to \"{body}.{timestamp}\" in one repo left every suite green while every customer's verification broke. These signatures are fixed bytes, independently reproduced with OpenSSL and Python — nothing here is derived from the code under test. reversed_order_* is the SAME input under the flipped concatenation: a verifier must reject it.",
